  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\u27e8t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{1-t}\u27e9 \\\\ g(t) & =\u27e82t-{t}^{2},\\,2t-1,\\,3\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,t,\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,{t}^{2},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}{e}^{1-t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,{1}^{2},{e}^{1-1}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,1,1\u27e9 \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(2t-{t}^{2}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(2t-1),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82(1)-{1}^{2},2(1)-1,3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,1,3\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =\u27e81,1,1\u27e9\\cdot \u27e81,1,3\u27e9 \\\\  & =1(1)+1(1)+1(3) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
